  "solution": "The logic here follows is:\n\n**(1st number)³ + 2nd number = 3rd Number**\n\n**1. (6, 12, 228)**\n\n**⇒ **6³ + 12 = 228\n\n⇒ 216 + 12 = 228\n\n⇒ 228 = 228\n\n2. (8, 3, 515)\n\n⇒ 8³ + 3 = 515\n\n⇒ 512 + 3 = 515 \n\n⇒ 515 = 515\n\nBy checking the options,\n\n1. (3, 28, 56)\n\n⇒ 33 + 28 = 56\n\n⇒ 27 + 28 = 56\n\n⇒ **55 ≠ 56**\n\n**2. (13, 11, 172)**\n\n⇒ 13³ + 11 = 172\n\n⇒ 2197 + 11 = 172\n\n⇒ **2208 ≠ 172**\n\n**3. (4, 18, 82)**\n\n⇒ 4³ + 18 = 82\n\n⇒ 64 + 18 = 82\n\n⇒ **82 = 82**\n\n**4. (9, 23, 119)**\n\n⇒ 9³ + 23 = 119\n\n⇒ 729 + 23 = 119\n\n⇒ **752 ≠ 119**\n\nHence the correct answer is **(4, 18, 82).**",
